    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor; read spec FR-16 (and FR-16), the create-surface inventory in notes/design-review-2026-10-19.md, CreateInvoiceWizard/invoiceService.ts, and the existing tests listed in relevant-files. Re-grep the line numbers cited here before editing (they are approximate).</step>
    <step order="1">Inventory keys on the invoice `entity`; classify user-entered vs client default; move defaults to the Invoice row of the task-012 registry or drop; list in task notes.</step>
    <step order="2">Delete the applyFieldMappings call (~:254) and import (~:38).</step>
    <step order="3">Keep the BFF create (~:270 via _dataService); add mappingSource only when the filed-under parent differs from the intended mapping source.</step>
    <step order="4">Add invoiceService.payload.test.ts (payload = user-entered keys only, no mapping call); run all CreateInvoiceWizard jest tests.</step>
    <step order="5">Build library and src/solutions/CreateInvoiceWizard; deploy via code-page-deploy (sprk_createinvoicewizard); live check per ui-tests.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Invoice row in the registry does not mark mapping-applies, STOP and escalate to task 012's owner rather than leaving invoices unmapped.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>invoiceService.resolver.test.ts covers the regarding resolver only; no existing test asserts the create payload.</existing>
    <extension>Extending the resolver test would mix concerns; the payload assertion is the FR-16 acceptance proof and needs its own focused file.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it nothing stops a client default or mapped key from creeping back into the invoice payload.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Invoice wizard renders"><steps><step>Open the Invoice wizard code page on dev from its launch command</step><step>Step through to the last step</step></steps><expected>All steps render with no console errors; Fluent v9 styling intact.</expected></test>
    <test name="Invoice create flow"><steps><step>Fill the required fields and click Finish</step></steps><expected>The record is created through POST /api/v1/child-records/{table}; the success state shows the new record; no direct Xrm.WebApi create call for the table.</expected></test>
    <test name="Mapped values visible on first load"><steps><step>Create the record under a parent that has an active field-mapping profile</step><step>Open the new record immediately (first load, no refresh or save)</step></steps><expected>Every field the active Mapping Profile maps from the parent is populated on the new record at first load; no client write filled them.</expected></test>
    <test name="User value preserved"><steps><step>Type a value into a field the profile also maps</step><step>Finish and open the record</step></steps><expected>The user's own value is stored; the mapped value did not overwrite it (fill-only, FR-02).</expected></test>
    <test name="ADR-021 dark mode"><steps><step>Switch the host to dark mode (theme toggle or prefers-color-scheme)</step><step>Open the wizard and step through every step</step></steps><expected>No unreadable text, no hard-coded light backgrounds, focus rings visible.</expected></test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools><tool name="npm">Build/test the code page and shared library</tool><tool name="code-page-deploy">Deploy the wizard web resource to dev</tool><tool name="ui-test">Browser verification on dev</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateInvoiceWizard/invoiceService.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateInvoiceWizard/__tests__/invoiceService.payload.test.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">invoiceService.ts has no applyFieldMappings call or import (grep).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">invoiceService.payload.test.ts proves the payload contains only user-entered values.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Invoice is created through the BFF route (no direct Xrm create).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: with a user value and a mapped value for the same field, the user value is stored; a mapped field the user never touched is populated on first load of the new record; the wizard payload contains no key the user did not enter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Deployed to dev via code-page-deploy; live check recorded in the task notes (mapped fields present on first load, user values kept, owner = owning team per FR-09); rollback bundle noted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`applyFieldMappings` no longer appears in CreateInvoiceWizard/invoiceService.ts; jest for the shared library and the host build pass; no existing test outside this wizard changes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-16. Office Invoice quick-create is task 018, not this task.</notes>

